HST Office: VBA conditional compilation, Debug.Print, Option Compare Text, compile on demand.

Found running real macro files; each one stopped or changed many macros:
- #If, #ElseIf, #Else, #End If and #Const were skipped, so both branches compiled, and a Declare in each
  branch of #If VBA7 stopped the module with "already defined" (20% of files use #If). Now only the
  branch that applies compiles; VBA6, VBA7, Win32 and Win64 are true, as in 64-bit Office for Windows.
- Debug.Print (18% of files) failed with "object not set" and Debug.Print a; b did not compile. The
  expressions now run; the text goes nowhere, as there is no Immediate window. Debug.Assert too.
- Option Compare Text had no effect on Like, =, <>, InStr and the other text functions.
- One compile error in any module stopped every macro of the project. As in VBA's compile on demand, it now
  only stops macros started from that module, which report it.


Also from the same measurement:
- Filter was missing.
- SaveSetting, GetSetting, DeleteSetting keep settings in a file in the user profile.
- FormatNumber groups digits by default, as in Excel.
- Collection.Add with a key in use gives error 457.
- Print # writes numbers with VBA's blanks: none before a minus sign, one after.
- Match is a real object: Match.SubMatches(1) works.


License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/vba-corpus/language_cases.py, regression_cases.py.
